WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.870
Morgan receives a polished Session

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.660
Option Brief.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.420
It compares three notes and says the

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.830
facilitator is confirmed.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.190
That one word is wrong.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.270
The source said ‘available for review.’

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:14.868
The preparation role did what an old brief told
it to do: 'Summarize the best session option.'

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.855
That sentence left the hardest part in Morgan's
head.

00:00:18.153 --> 00:00:19.263
What counts as ready?

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.820
Which source is required?

00:00:21.097 --> 00:00:22.389
When must the work stop?

00:00:22.614 --> 00:00:24.192
A human colleague might ask.

00:00:24.363 --> 00:00:27.414
A paper agent design needs those answers
written down.

00:00:27.764 --> 00:00:31.658
Chapter Eleven turns the request into an
Agentic PRD Packet.

00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:40.865
Seven fields carry the load: outcome, scope
fences, input manifest, acceptance tests,
escalation, owner, and reversal.

00:00:41.142 --> 00:00:45.164
The outcome is a comparison Morgan can review,
not a session announcement.

00:00:45.388 --> 00:00:49.633
Scope fences keep the role away from
participant messages and calendar changes.

00:00:49.953 --> 00:00:54.602
The input manifest lists the three Harbor note
references and their freshness checks.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.574
An acceptance test says staffing language must
match the facilitator note exactly in meaning.

00:01:00.788 --> 00:01:04.990
If the note is missing or ambiguous, the
escalation is a hold for Morgan.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.971
Reversal is modest here.

00:01:07.237 --> 00:01:10.949
Morgan can return a draft for correction or
withdraw it from review.

00:01:11.333 --> 00:01:13.509
There is no external send to reverse.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:21.455
A test result belongs beside the draft as
evidence: source IDs checked, staffing wording
checked, review gate present.

00:01:21.763 --> 00:01:25.603
A failed check does not become a footnote under
a confident recommendation.

00:01:25.859 --> 00:01:27.288
It blocks the handoff.

00:01:27.608 --> 00:01:32.174
This packet remains a proposed design; writing
it does not configure an agent.

00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:34.196
Now give the work an organization.

00:01:34.545 --> 00:01:39.536
One role checks sources; one role assembles the
comparison; Morgan owns the outcome.

00:01:39.707 --> 00:01:47.311
If both preparation roles produce separate
answers without a common handoff, Morgan gets a
small swarm and two versions of the truth.

00:01:47.576 --> 00:01:53.976
Chapter Twelve's Pod Model asks for a charter,
lead, specialists, board, standup, and handoff.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:59.608
For this tiny classroom pod, keep the lead as a
preparation coordinator, not an approver.

00:01:59.949 --> 00:02:02.646
The board is a proposed paper status list.

00:02:03.038 --> 00:02:06.643
The standup is a short proposed summary of
ready and blocked work.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:11.175
The charter is narrow: prepare one
evidence-bound option brief for Morgan.

00:02:11.516 --> 00:02:16.199
The source checker may flag staleness, not
repair a source by inventing a newer date.

00:02:16.486 --> 00:02:19.409
The drafter may compare, not confirm staffing.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.782
The coordinator may route a blocked packet to
Morgan, not override the block.

00:02:24.081 --> 00:02:26.461
The board should show who holds the next move.

00:02:26.793 --> 00:02:30.548
If nobody owns a failed source check, the org
chart is decorative.

00:02:30.847 --> 00:02:33.087
Write that ownership into the handoff now.

00:02:33.437 --> 00:02:33.906
Pause.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:37.853
Who would receive the brief if the facilitator
note stays unconfirmed?

00:02:38.173 --> 00:02:39.766
Name the role and the human.

00:02:40.116 --> 00:02:42.868
Draft the seven-field PRD in under a page.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:48.564
Give it two acceptance tests, including the
staffing claim, and one explicit failure route.

00:02:48.777 --> 00:02:56.311
Then sketch the Pod Model: charter, lead,
specialists, board, standup, handoff, and human
owner.

00:02:56.549 --> 00:02:58.575
Use role labels and course references.

00:02:58.853 --> 00:03:00.943
Use a fictional or approved example.

00:03:01.199 --> 00:03:08.420
Do not use private operational data, configure
production agents, or promote the pod's
coordinator into final decision authority.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.053
Save revision seven as a draft.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:04:02.080
A requirement becomes useful when a new
teammate can tell what to prepare and when to
stop.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:04.040
A team becomes useful when a blocked

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.590
packet has one place to land.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.190
Next we will test that handoff with

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.270
three course cases.
